Package: bitcoin-core
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Bitcoin Core server binaries (DWDC signet build)
 Bitcoin Core, built from the upstream release tag with one local patch.
 .
 Contains the server components only: bitcoind, bitcoin-cli and
 bitcoin-util. The GUI and the test binaries are not built.
 .
 LOCAL PATCH: adds -signetblocktime, which lets the difficulty adjustment
 target a chosen block time on a custom signet. Without it, a signet
 mined faster than ten minutes retargets upward every 2016 blocks until
 it drifts back to ten-minute blocks. The patch is benthecarman's,
 offered to Bitcoin Core as PR #27446 and closed unmerged in January
 2024; Bitcoin Knots carries it as d8434da3c1. It touches signet chain
 parameters only and changes nothing on mainnet, testnet or regtest.
 .
 This means the package is NOT stock Bitcoin Core. A node built from the
 upstream tag alone cannot follow a signet that uses a non-default block
 time, which is the same tradeoff Mutinynet makes.
 .
 Built from source by DWDC for testing and development. The signature on
 this package attests that DWDC built it from the named upstream tag plus
 the patch above; it is not a reproducible build and does not attest that
 the binaries match those published by the Bitcoin Core project.
